---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  title="No Human Left Behind"
  description="The mission underneath the work. A commitment to building a future where technology, ethics, and humanity move forward together, with nobody left behind."
>
  <article class="nhlb">
    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="section-cream section" aria-labelledby="nhlb-heading">
      <div class="container container-narrow">
        <p class="label label-gold">The North Star</p>
        <h1 id="nhlb-heading" class="nhlb-title">No Human Left Behind</h1>
        <p class="nhlb-statement">
          A commitment to building a future where technology, ethics, and
          humanity move forward together, with nobody left behind.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- The commitment -->
    <section class="section-dark section" aria-labelledby="commit-heading">
      <div class="container container-narrow">
        <p class="label nhlb-label">The Commitment</p>
        <h2 id="commit-heading" class="nhlb-section-heading">A tension I live with daily</h2>
        <div class="prose nhlb-prose">
          <p>
            I love AI. I am a power user. It has changed the way I think, build,
            and create, and I want others to experience that.
          </p>
          <p>
            I am also deeply aware of the damage it can cause. To jobs, to
            creativity, to human connection. I have struggled with this, and it
            is not resolved.
          </p>
          <p>
            That tension is my engine. I take everything that keeps me up at
            night about AI and build it into frameworks, tools, and ways of
            working that keep humans at the center of AI adoption.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- The core tension -->
    <section class="section-cream section" aria-labelledby="tension-heading">
      <div class="container container-narrow">
        <p class="label label-gold">What It Is, and Is Not</p>
        <h2 id="tension-heading" class="nhlb-section-heading">Hold both truths, build anyway</h2>
        <p class="nhlb-body">
          This is not anti-AI doomerism, and it is not uncritical AI hype. It is
          something harder: using the thing you are worried about, responsibly,
          while helping others do the same. The goal is not to resolve the
          tension. It is to hold both truths and build anyway.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- How it becomes practice -->
    <section class="section-dark section" aria-labelledby="practice-heading">
      <div class="container container-narrow">
        <p class="label nhlb-label">How It Becomes Practice</p>
        <h2 id="practice-heading" class="nhlb-section-heading">Three methods, one mission</h2>
        <p class="nhlb-prose-lead">
          A commitment is only as good as what it changes on a Tuesday. These
          three carry it into the work.
        </p>
        <div class="nhlb-methods">
          <div class="nhlb-method">
            <h3 class="nhlb-method-name">
              <a href="/frameworks/the-lift" class="link-light">The Lift</a>
            </h3>
            <p class="nhlb-method-desc">
              How a whole team adopts AI without leaving its slower adopters,
              its skeptics, or its non-engineers behind.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="nhlb-method">
            <h3 class="nhlb-method-name">
              <a href="/frameworks/encoding-intent" class="link-light">Encoding Intent</a>
            </h3>
            <p class="nhlb-method-desc">
              How a person stays in control of AI work, by putting human
              judgment in first, before the model writes anything.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="nhlb-method">
            <h3 class="nhlb-method-name">
              <a href="/frameworks/four-lenses" class="link-light">The Four Lenses</a>
            </h3>
            <p class="nhlb-method-desc">
              How to check whether an AI tool actually serves the people using
              it, and the people affected by it, before it scales.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</PageLayout>

<style>
  .nhlb-title {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: var(--text-4xl);
    line-height: 1.1;
  }

  .nhlb-statement {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: var(--text-2xl);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.35;
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
    max-width: var(--max-width-prose);
  }

  .nhlb-section-heading {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: var(--text-3xl);
    line-height: 1.15;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .nhlb-label {
    color: var(--color-gold);
  }

  .nhlb-body,
  .nhlb-prose-lead {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    max-width: var(--max-width-prose);
  }

  .nhlb-prose-lead {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .nhlb-methods {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-lg);
    max-width: var(--max-width-prose);
  }

  .nhlb-method {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-gray-border-dark, rgba(245, 243, 238, 0.2));
    padding-top: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .nhlb-method-name {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: var(--text-2xl);
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2xs);
  }

  .nhlb-method-desc {
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }
</style>
